{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The subject's application-neutral traversal-occurrence profile defines record, relation, identity, causal, effect-boundary, frontier and refusal laws. It supplies no operational or judgment authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1443,
          "quote":"This profile owns only the application-neutral record, relation, identity,\ncausal, effect-boundary, frontier and refusal laws above.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FAuthority%20and%20adoption",
          "start_line":1438
        }
      ],
      "key":"occurrence_profile",
      "label":"Traversal-occurrence profile"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"RefDomain_Sigma_occurrence(record_kind, qualified_field) is the profile's complete finite reference-domain specialization. Source populations are exactly O/E/C/L/X/V/T/J; O:S denotes sort S; AnyLocal is their closed union; Sigma:K denotes one exact member of a named closed signature population. Empty cells allow no target of that class. Sigma:ReferenceDomain, Sigma:ExternalTargetKind and Sigma:BasisRelation belong to this profile, not the calculus. B_model means the same M_occ,b and record basis; B_profile exact TraversalOccurrenceProfileBasis resolution; B_calculus exact imported AxiomaticCalculusBasis resolution; B_adopted the exact Product-adoption basis relation named for the external kind.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":266,
          "quote":"The basis codes are exact relations, not labels (P3):",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20semantic-object%20sorts%2FFinite%20reference-domain%20table",
          "start_line":260
        },
        {
          "end_line":258,
          "quote":"`Sigma:ReferenceDomain`, `Sigma:ExternalTargetKind` and\n`Sigma:BasisRelation` are populations of this profile's signature, named\nhere and not by the calculus (P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20semantic-object%20sorts%2FFinite%20reference-domain%20table",
          "start_line":256
        }
      ],
      "key":"reference_domains",
      "label":"Finite reference domains and basis relations"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"ProfileRecordRef is the closed union of profile semantic-object records O and the exact inherited E, C, L, X, V, T and J populations in the same model. It creates no ninth record kind. The inherited names include TypedRelation, Traversal, transformation and Judgment.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":584,
          "quote":"`ProfileRecordRef` is the closed union of the profile semantic-object\nrecords in `O` and the exact inherited `E`, `C`, `L`, `X`, `V`, `T` and `J`\npopulations in the same model; it introduces no ninth record kind.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20relation%20families",
          "start_line":582
        }
      ],
      "key":"profile_record",
      "label":"ProfileRecordRef and inherited record populations"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
