        }
      ],
      "key":"relation_claim",
      "label":"RelationClaim"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"FrameworkEvent binds a declared event kind, unchanged payload and digest, source frontier and scope-dependent occurrence and claim fields. The exact closed event-kind identities are urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:claim-admission, urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:occurrence-admission, urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:effect-disposition and urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:external-fact-admission.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":532,
          "quote":"EventKind_occurrence = {\n  urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:claim-admission,\n  urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:occurrence-admission,\n  urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:effect-disposition,\n  urn:stdo:traversal-occurrence:event-kind:external-fact-admission\n}",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20event-kind%20population",
          "start_line":527
        }
      ],
      "key":"framework_event",
      "label":"FrameworkEvent and event kinds"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"EventFrontier binds the complete evaluated event population, exact basis and declared precedence law. Projection immutably identifies one unchanged frontier, projection rule, selected relations, boundaries and residuals.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1413,
          "quote":"An `EventFrontier` binds the complete member set of events evaluated, its\nexact basis and its declared precedence law. A projection judgment points\nto one unchanged `Projection` identity and digest, and that projection\nbinds exactly one unchanged frontier (P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FEvent%20frontier%20and%20projection",
          "start_line":1410
        }
      ],
      "key":"frontier_and_projection",
      "label":"EventFrontier and Projection"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"SemanticAdmissionCut is the seven-member tuple of unchanged claim, claim judgment, event, event judgment, materialized relation, source frontier and successor frontier; a separate cut judgment judges that tuple.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1148,
          "quote":"  -> SemanticAdmissionCut a = (c, j_c, e, j_e, r, F_k, F_k_plus_1)\n  -> Judgment j_a over unchanged a",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FCandidate%2C%20judgment%2C%20event%20and%20relation%20separation",
          "start_line":1147
        }
      ],
      "key":"semantic_admission_cut",
      "label":"SemanticAdmissionCut"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"EffectSubject binds the occurrence, subject binding, pre-observation, invocation, operation, grant, territory and currentness invalidation for readiness. TransitionSubject binds occurrence, subject binding, pre-observation, optional post-observation, intended outcome, disposition and bounded effect evidence for transition evaluation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":372,
          "quote":"| `O:EffectSubject.value.pre_observation_ref` | 1 | `O` | `Observation` |  | `B_model` |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20semantic-object%20sorts%2FFinite%20reference-domain%20table",
          "start_line":360
        }
      ],
      "key":"effect_and_transition_subject",
      "label":"EffectSubject and TransitionSubject"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The closed relation signature comprises the 24 kinds application_of, applies_traversal, bound_to_subject, intends, observes_before, observes_after, invokes_effect, operation_of_kind, targets_subject, authorized_by, disposition_for, evidenced_by, event_for, frontier_contains, projects_frontier, identity_depends_on, causally_precedes_occurrence, causally_precedes_event, supports_event, corrects_event, component_of_occurrence, admits_claim, materializes_relation and transition_for. Each is an exact inherited TypedRelation with OccurrenceRelationQualifiers.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":591,
          "quote":"Each relation is an exact `TypedRelation`. Its qualifiers close direction,\ncardinality, basis, preservation, refusal and invalidation semantics; the\ntable is no permission to omit inherited relation fields.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20relation%20families",
          "start_line":588
        }
      ],
      "key":"occurrence_relation_signature",
      "label":"Closed relation kinds and qualifiers"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Core constraint kinds: identity_dependency_acyclic, occurrence_causation_acyclic, event_causation_acyclic, occurrence_seed_complete, relation_claim_admissible, semantic_cut_complete, pre_effect_current, operation_grant_contains_effect, event_scope_compatible, frontier_complete, transition_subject_complete. Judgment kinds: model_validation, occurrence_admission, event_admission, claim_admission, semantic_cut_admission, effect_readiness, transition_evaluation, frontier_projection. Residual kinds: unobserved_subject_state, partial_effect, unresolved_cause, unresolved_scope, competing_lineage, stale_frontier, stale_currentness, unobserved_external_mutation. Stop kinds: hold, gap, refusal, invalid_basis, out_of_scope, partial_effect. These are source-defined categories, not emitted judgments or stops of this interpretation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":775,
          "quote":"The core constraint kinds are (P3, P5):",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20constraint%2C%20judgment%2C%20residual%20and%20stop%20kinds",
          "start_line":724
        }
      ],
      "key":"occurrence_result_domains",
      "label":"Constraint, judgment, residual and stop domains"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Three distinct graphs are G_id, the identity-dependency DAG; G_occ_cause, the declared occurrence-causation DAG; and G_evt_cause, the declared event-causation DAG. Wider typed lineage includes evidential support, correction and composition without thereby asserting cause.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1260,
          "quote":"G_id          identity-dependency DAG\nG_occ_cause   declared occurrence-causation DAG\nG_evt_cause   declared event-causation DAG",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FCausality%20and%20typed%20lineage",
          "start_line":1258
        }
      ],
      "key":"typed_lineage",
      "label":"Identity, causation and wider typed lineage"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The stable concept urn:stdo:concept:traversal-occurrence-profile does not identify an immutable edition. TraversalOccurrenceSignature and TraversalOccurrenceProfileBasis bind an edition through exact canonical signature, calculus basis and immutable publication bytes.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1466,
          "quote":"The stable concept identity does not identify one immutable profile\nedition. Once publication bytes exist, the signature preimage is issued as\nbelow (P3, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FExact%20profile%20identity",
          "start_line":1464
        }
      ],
      "key":"profile_publication_identity",
      "label":"Exact profile signature and basis identity"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The source-disposition account reports reception of all 25 rc.2 TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md rows under STDO-UP-015. Routes and predecessor coordinates are provenance, not authority or edition identity; conservation and supersession are source claims.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1665,
          "quote":"Rows of rc.2 TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md received by this member, all\n25 under STDO-UP-015. Anchors are into rc.2\nTRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md; a locus is a section of this file. Every\nconserved row is restated in this member's own text at the predecessor's\nmodal force; a route is provenance only.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FSource%20dispositions",
          "start_line":1661
        }
      ],
      "key":"occurrence_source_dispositions",
      "label":"Occurrence-profile source disposition account"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"UX is an optional Tier 3 profile, material family F20, refining DESIGN_MODULE for modules realizing UX surfaces. Its own terms include UX surface, State, Msg, Update, View, ViewTree, Cmd, Sub, view-local ephemera, effect membrane, product-truth-changing message, admitted product carrier, Msg-replay test/proof, scaffold, exemption record, UX sprint and refined results. Graph function and ABG belong to the graph-execution profile; AssetSurface and workorder name Product-designed carriers.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":15,
          "quote":"Tier 3. An optional profile for realising UX surfaces:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/UX.md#UX",
          "start_line":3
        },
        {
          "end_line":35,
          "quote":"This profile's own terms are UX surface, State, Msg, Update, View,\nViewTree, Cmd and Sub (§4), view-local ephemera (§5), effect membrane\n(§6), product-truth-changing message and admitted product carrier (§3),\nMsg-replay test and Msg-replay proof (§8), scaffold and exemption record\n(§12), UX sprint (§12) and the refined result values of §15.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/UX.md#UX",
          "start_line":27
        }
      ],
      "key":"ux_profile",
      "label":"UX profile"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Elm Architecture process model: State is typed runtime-held state; Msg is the typed algebra naming every user/system action; Update is the pure (Msg, State) → (State, Cmd) reducer; View is the pure State → ViewTree function with identical output for identical state; Cmd and Sub describe scheduled effects and external subscriptions interpreted by the runtime at the effect membrane. The runtime owns rendering, message reduction, effect interpretation and repetition, including lifecycle and continuation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":268,
          "quote":"- Update: the pure reducer of signature `(Msg, State) → (State, Cmd)`; it\n  describes side effects as Cmd values and does not perform them;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F4.%20Process%20model",
          "start_line":262
        },
        {
          "end_line":272,
          "quote":"`current State → render View → user emits Msg → Update produces new State and Cmds → runtime interprets Cmds → repeat`",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F4.%20Process%20model",
          "start_line":272
        }
      ],
      "key":"ux_process_model",
      "label":"Elm process model and its typed coordinates"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"UX surfaces render admitted product truth and emit typed control messages. Product-truth-changing messages require one admitted product carrier: an AssetSurface action; published graph function or lawful composition; design-admitted workorder/job/runtime command; ABG event/command boundary where ABG has runtime authority; or another typed Product contract named by the design module.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":247,
          "quote":"Such a message maps to one admitted product carrier (P6, P4a):",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F3.%20Product%20truth%20and%20admitted%20carriers",
          "start_line":241
        }
