      "key":"ux_stack_documentation_and_tests",
      "statement":"The process model is constitutional and non-negotiable; project-local stack choice is free only while preserving it. Record framework choice with a short model-preservation justification, and each realization choice with a short justification against both Elm §4 and membrane §6. The profile tests realizations rather than ranking stacks. One supplied compliance statement accepts preserving §§4–8; Realisation discretion instead requires §§4–10 under inspection and absence of §13 failures. Both explicitly acknowledge the difference and a pending Product-owner ruling; the supplied foundation row states the stricter test applies meanwhile. Reject view-owned continuation, render effects, state mutation outside typed reduction, multi-step view-local state machines bypassing Msg, two-way bindings without Msg, imperative render DOM manipulation and controller-like effect handlers regardless of stack, retaining the explicit §5 local-ephemera allowance.",
